<title>POLAND: Polish pork prices flat last week - agency.</title>
<headline>Polish pork prices flat last week - agency.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's food market regulator, the Agriculture Market Agency (ARR), sold 3,070 tonnes of frozen pork on Polish markets last week at an unchanged average price of 4.50 zlotys/kg, the agency said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The agency said in a statement last week's minimum price was 4.02 zlotys/kg in the south-eastern city of Lublin, while the maximum price was 4.68 zlotys/kg in Warsaw.</p>
<p>The ARR has sold over 35,000 tonnes of pork in its intervention on the market since July to curb the rapid growth of prices which peaked at over five zlotys/kg in August. --Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
